      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i got a tenant complaining that one of the bedrooms in her house is staying really hot even though the AC is running constantly. the rest of the house seems fine. can u give me a list of common reasons why one room might not be cooling properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A hot bedroom, even with the AC running, is a frustrating problem. One of the most common culprits is poor insulation or air leaks around that specific room. It's also possible that the room is getting too much direct sunlight, which can heat it up faster than the AC can compensate. Sometimes, an appliance or even a poorly sealed window can be the sneaky source of the heat gain. You might want to check the window seals first, as those are often the easiest fix.",
